<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Translucent backing for the flight screen's HUD text blocks (operator, 2026-08-04).

     WHY: the readouts sit over live video whose brightness the pilot does not control. Over dark
     terrain the white text is fine; over snow, wet asphalt or a white roof it washes out, and the
     drop-shadow in flightReadoutText is not enough on its own. A fixed backing means legibility
     no longer depends on what the camera happens to be pointing at.

     WHY THIS LIGHT: this covers live video the pilot is flying from, and the HUD column overlaps
     the right-hand side of the image. At full opacity these panels would be two solid blind spots.
     Started at 55% black, lightened to 40% (operator, 2026-08-04), then to 20% (operator,
     2026-08-15) — enough to lift the text off a bright background, light enough to still see
     movement through it. If the readouts ever wash out over snow, raise this rather than making
     the text bigger. The value is tp_hud_panel_scrim; change it there, not here.

     Corners and padding are deliberately modest — this is meant to read as a wash behind the text,
     not as a card sitting on top of the video. -->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">

    <solid android:color="@color/tp_hud_panel_scrim" />

    <corners android:radius="6dp" />

    <padding
        android:left="8dp"
        android:top="6dp"
        android:right="8dp"
        android:bottom="6dp" />
</shape>
